From 36587ea3573685b684af08bc2ebc038af5771a3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 01:03:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build 80-chart sports analytics dashboard on real TheSportsDB
 data

- Data layer: season, round, league-detail and seasons endpoints in
  ApiConfig; in-memory cache with shared in-flight requests; soccer-only
  league list; 429/"No data"/empty-body handling; on-demand, rate-limited
  completion of truncated seasons via eventsround.
- Analytics: SeasonAnalytics computes standings, home/away splits, rounds
  and per-round position history once per load; team/match mappers derive
  every metric locally from scored matches (no simulated data).
- Charts: reusable Syncfusion components (CategoryChart, ranking, XY with
  trendlines, circular, range, hilo, histogram, box plot, waterfall) and a
  declarative catalog of 80 charts in 10 categories. Radar/polar is not
  available in Syncfusion, so radial bar and normalized grouped columns
  replace it.
- UI: dashboard with side navigation / mobile chips, league search,
  season, team and multi-team selectors with badges, Top/Bottom filters,
  calculated standings table, recent results and per-chart empty/error
  states. The three original charts are kept in the catalog.
- Tests: calculations, filters, empty/unscored data, JSON parsing,
  repository cache and round completion, dashboard flow with a mocked
  HTTP client, and rendering of all 80 charts.
- pubspec.lock no longer lists fl_chart/charts_flutter.

